/code-review high — R7 round 2 — range b14ada40..eb3b78eb

I found 9 issues in this round. Three of them are new problems in the fixes themselves:

- **`require_pin_source` misreads the fragment in two ways.** It can't read the escaped strings setup now writes. It also silently skips any line with a trailing comment.
- **The task's own fix instruction is wrong for an upgraded repo.** A user who follows it has their committed pin replaced by whatever this machine detects.
- **The ux-gate audit misses the new override check.** When an old `mise.toml` pin overrides the fragment, the audit runs on that stale simulator while `test:golden` refuses.

Four round-1 findings are still in the tree. The run log dropped them as belonging to other units, and they aren't in the plan's Gaps list:

- **The `sh -c '<detect>'` wording breaks every shipped detect.** A literal reading of the quoting fails all four detect commands, and doctor's probe line has the same wording.
- **stackgen-sync can overwrite the filled pins with empty values.** On the next swiftui pack bump it treats the fragment as "pack moved" and selects it by default.
- **The `lockfile:` fact never reaches a SwiftUI repo's check.** It is declared on swiftpm, which only ships inside project-axis bundles, while doctor reads it under `repo.stack`.
- **A Mac-only app's empty device and OS pins are offered an iPhone on every setup run.** Every run also re-asks all four questions.

The last two (the checker accepting `machine_env` with no fragment, and the missing lockfile in a repo with no dependencies) are already recorded as G4. I kept them at the bottom because they are still defects.

